  "observations": [
    "All three seeds froze after epoch 4 and produced similar beta distributions: approximately 78-80% sharing coverage and mean beta between 0.507 and 0.548.",
    "Soft sharing achieved the highest three-seed mean validation macro accuracy among the evaluated row-sharing methods, winning against all-row hard sharing on two of three seeds.",
    "The gain over all-row hard sharing is small (0.1271 percentage points), so three seeds do not establish decisive superiority.",
    "The macro improvement comes primarily from ER; KS and SI decrease slightly relative to all-row hard sharing.",
    "Unlike gated hard sharing at seeds 43 and 44, no soft-sharing run showed a late finite-loss explosion.",
    "Frozen-pair match rates declined after sharing, but frozen assignments and beta values did not change; this measures counterfactual nearest-pair agreement rather than assignment mutation."
  ],
  "decision": "The 0.05-to-0.20 soft-sharing rule is a stable and promising macro-oriented configuration. It is suitable for a 100-epoch comparison, but should not yet be claimed as universally better than all-row hard sharing."
